<section class="introduction">
      <div><h1>Encoded in the sky</h1><p class="lead">Astrolabe B preserves a Babylonian list assigning three celestial names to each of the twelve months, one in each of the paths of Enlil, Anu and Ea. This atlas compares those monthly assignments with modern star positions.</p></div>
      <div class="intro-note"><span class="note-rule"></span><p>“He set up three stars each<br>for the twelve months.”</p><span>ENŪMA ELIŠ · TABLET V · ADAPTED</span></div>
    </section>
